{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Progress 2026-11-11 19:40 PST (session 3d705fec), worktree .rebar/worktrees/fix-fulmar.\nRoot cause (measured): GIT_TRACE2_EVENT of the fixture's raw `git commit` (git 2.56.0) records one child, `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach`. git's maintenance_run_tasks (builtin/gc.c) takes <objects>/maintenance.lock before checking any task's auto condition, then daemonize()s while holding it; the background child's rollback_lock_file unlinks the path. So the commit returns while a daemon owns that lock, and a test that writes the lock in that window has it deleted under it: exactly the FileNotFoundError at line 254. Change 3351 does not interact (it covers only run_git_bounded/run_git_reaped; this test never invokes the CLI).\nFix (commit e465ea285c4): _cli_tracker applies the existing shared pins (tests/_git_upkeep.apply_upkeep_pins: gc/maintenance autoDetach=false), the same fix class bare remotes already use. New guard test traces the fixture under a forced-detach GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL with GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1: an unpinned control records a --detach maintenance child, the pinned fixture records upkeep but none detached. Mutation check: removing the pin call turns the guard RED (assert [['git','mai...','--detach']] == []), restoring it GREEN. Stress: the module plus the flaky test, 200 rounds under -n 4, 200/200 passed (19:24-19:36 PST). No config key, env var, flag or helper added. make verify running outside the sandbox."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794454714783833487,"uuid":"a0e57a5e-f201-4446-83af-69267d03f59d"}